# VS-13 S2 (2026-05-04): public/cesium/ is generated by
# scripts/copy-cesium-assets.mjs (predev/prebuild). ~3 MB of cesium
# Workers + Assets + Widgets + ThirdParty; not tracked.
public/cesium/

# I-15 (issue #70, closed by tsconfig `noEmit: true`): the patterns
# below were originally a workaround for `tsc -b` emitting .js / .js.map
# / .d.ts next to source. tsconfig.json now sets `noEmit: true`, so any
# tsc invocation (including IDE / editor TS server in build mode) is
# guaranteed not to emit. We keep the patterns as a defensive backstop —
# a future override (someone running `tsc --noEmit false` directly, or
# a misconfigured editor plugin) will still be caught before commit.
#
# VS-13 S1.1 follow-up: src/types/ holds INTENTIONAL ambient
# declarations (CSS modules, @fontsource side-effect imports). The
# `!src/types/**` carve-out keeps legitimate .d.ts tracked.
src/**/*.js
src/**/*.js.map
src/**/*.d.ts
!src/types/**
vite.config.js
